[{"text":"CartesianMomentum[p] is the head of a 3-momentum p. The internal representation of a 3-dimensional p is CartesianMomentum[p]. For other than three dimensions: CartesianMomentum[p, Dimension]. CartesianMomentum[p, 3] simplifies to CartesianMomentum[p].","anchor":"cartesianmomentum"},{"text":"Overview, Momentum, TemporalMomentum.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"This is a 3-dimensional momentum","anchor":"examples","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CartesianMomentum[p]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"As an optional second argument the dimension must be specified if it is different from 3","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CartesianMomentum[p, D - 1]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[p\\]","anchor":"cb2-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"The dimension index is suppressed in the output.","anchor":"cb2-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CartesianMomentum[p, d - 1]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[p\\]","anchor":"cb3-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"a1 = CartesianMomentum[-q]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-\\overline{q}\\]","anchor":"cb4-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"a1 // StandardForm (*-CartesianMomentum[q]*)","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"a2 = CartesianMomentum[p - q] + CartesianMomentum[2 q]","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\overline{p}-\\overline{q}\\right)+2 \\overline{q}\\]","anchor":"cb6-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"a2 // StandardForm (*CartesianMomentum[p - q] + 2 CartesianMomentum[q]*)","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"},{"text":"a2 // MomentumExpand // StandardForm (*CartesianMomentum[p] + CartesianMomentum[q]*)","anchor":"cb8","section":"Examples"},{"text":"a2 // MomentumCombine // StandardForm (*CartesianMomentum[p + q]*)","anchor":"cb9","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Notice that when changing the dimension, one must specify its value as if the the 3-vector were the spatial component of the corresponding 4-vector","anchor":"cb9-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ChangeDimension[CartesianMomentum[p], d - 1] // StandardForm (*CartesianMomentum[p, -2 + d]*)","anchor":"cb10","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ChangeDimension[CartesianMomentum[p], d] // StandardForm (*CartesianMomentum[p, -1 + d]*)","anchor":"cb11","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Clear[a1, a2]","anchor":"cb12","section":"Examples"}]